# expect-fail: Features are precomputed and read from an online store
# expect-fail: p99 of Load Explore < 300 ms
# mistake: Reading features from the offline warehouse on every request
# explain: A warehouse query takes about half a second and a warehouse node answers a few hundred a second, so 1k Explore loads a second saturate it and one query alone costs more than the latency budget.
# explain: Compute features offline in batches, load them into a key-value store or cache, and read them there in one batched call per request.
# lesson: precomputed-features-and-embeddings
# cards: recommendations-precomputed-features, oltp-vs-olap, slowest-operation
# No feature store: the Explore API asks the warehouse for the features of 500 posts on every request.
import "problem.proschi"

explore    "Explore API"         [gRPC]          x3 @serving "Runs retrieval, queries features and calls the rankers"
retrieval  "Candidate Retrieval" [Service]       x3 @serving "Samples 500 eligible posts from similar accounts"
embeddings "Account Embeddings"  [Search Engine] x2 @serving "Nearest-neighbour index over account embeddings"
light      "First-pass Ranker"   [gRPC]          x8 @ranking "Distilled model: 500 down to 150"
medium     "Second-pass Ranker"  [gRPC]          x10 @ranking "Lightweight network: 150 down to 50"
heavy      "Final Ranker"        [gRPC]          x15 @ranking "Deep network: 50 down to 25"

user      -> explore    : HTTPS
explore   -> retrieval  : gRPC
retrieval -> embeddings : KNN query
explore   -> warehouse  : SQL
explore   -> light      : gRPC
explore   -> medium     : gRPC
explore   -> heavy      : gRPC
pipeline  -> warehouse  : SQL
pipeline  -> embeddings : bulk load

usecase "Load Explore" "The features of each candidate are queried from the warehouse" {
  user        -> explore    : GET /explore
  explore     -> retrieval  : GET candidates for the user
  retrieval   -> embeddings : KNN accounts near the user's seed accounts
  embeddings --> retrieval  : similar accounts
  retrieval  --> explore    : 500 eligible posts from those accounts
  explore     -> warehouse  : SELECT features of 500 posts and of the user
  warehouse  --> explore    : features
  explore     -> light      : x500 SCORE with the distilled model
  light      --> explore    : best 150
  explore     -> medium     : x150 SCORE with the lightweight network
  medium     --> explore    : best 50
  explore     -> heavy      : x50 SCORE with the deep network
  heavy      --> explore    : best 25, ordered by expected value
  explore    --> user       : 200 page of 25 posts
}

usecase "Refresh features" "The offline pipeline rebuilds the embeddings in batches" {
  pipeline    -> warehouse  : SELECT a batch of recent interactions
  warehouse  --> pipeline   : rows
  pipeline    -> embeddings : UPSERT a batch of account embeddings
  embeddings --> pipeline   : ok
}
